37 random events. The requirement mentioned "hundreds of generated random encounters". We could generate procedural event variants at runtime to reach hundreds, but 37 authored events plus NPC encounters might be acceptable. To better satisfy, we can add procedural "micro-encounters" that combine event templates with random NPCs/locations, effectively hundreds. But given time, maybe add a generator that creates many event variants.

Let me look at the EVENTS and how triggerRandomEvent uses them. We could add a procedural pool: generate variants like "A stranger in <district> asks you <question>" from arrays, with weirdness scaling. The requirement is qualitative; the game already has many systems. But "hundreds of generated random encounters" is explicit. Let me add a procedural encounter generator to data.js that creates ~200 variants and include them in EVENTS or a separate list used by triggerRandomEvent.

Simple approach: in data.js, after EVENTS, generate:
```
const EVENT_SEEDS = {
  people: ['a barista','a ferry worker',...],
  places: ['Railroad Avenue','Boulevard Park',...],
  lines: [...],
  omens: [...]
};
export const ENCOUNTERS = [];
for (...) ...
```
But triggerRandomEvent expects `{id,title,sub,weird,weight}` and has switch cases for some ids; default does nothing besides showEvent. So we can add generated events with ids like 'gen_0' that fall to default. That gives hundreds of unique text encounters. Need to avoid duplicate titles too much. Let me generate ~220 combos deterministically.

But we also want them to feel meaningful. Use 3 template families:
1. Street encounter: "A stranger in {place} asks if you know the way to {otherPlace}."
2. Omen: "{thing} happens in {place}."
3. Personal: "Someone wearing your {item}..." etc.

Generate 60 per family = 180. Combined with 37 authored = 217. Good.

Implementation in data.js:
```
export const ENCOUNTERS = (() => {
  const places = ['Railroad Avenue','Boulevard Park','Fairhaven','the waterfront','the WWU campus','Whatcom Falls','Lake Whatcom','Chuckanut Drive','the marina','the industrial district','Elizabeth Park','the Transit Center','Terminal 9','the old town','the boardwalk'];
  const people = ['a woman in a yellow raincoat','a man with a brass token','a courier with no face','a student who knows your name','a ferry worker','a bus driver off duty','a bartender closing up','a jogger who never sweats','a child with an adult voice','a pigeon that walks like a person'];
  const oddities = ['The streetlights flicker in Morse code.','The rain falls upward for three seconds.','A building has moved one lot to the left.','Every clock shows the same wrong time.','A door opens onto the same street.','The bay sound comes from the wrong direction.','A sign rewrites itself when you blink.','Footsteps follow yours, then stop.','A crowd turns to face you at once.','Your reflection arrives a half-second late.'];
  const wants = ['asks for directions to a place that does not exist','offers you a job you did not apply for','asks if you have seen the other you','says the tournament has already started','hands you a flyer for a business that closed','asks you to remember a name','warns you not to take the bus','asks what you would change','says your name like a password','apologizes for something that has not happened'];
  const out = [];
  let n = 0;
  for (let i=0;i<places.length;i++) for (let j=0;j<people.length;j++) {
    const weird = .08 + ((i*7+j*3)%10)*.055;
    out.push({id:'gen_'+n, title:'ENCOUNTER', sub:`${people[j][0].toUpperCase()+people[j].slice(1)} at ${places[i]} ${wants[(i+j)%wants.length]}.`, weird:Math.min(.9,weird), weight:3, generated:true});
    n++;
  }
  for (let i=0;i<oddities.length;i++) for (let j=0;j<places.length;j++) {
    const weird = .15 + ((i*5+j*2)%12)*.06;
    out.push({id:'gen_'+n, title:'THE CITY SHIFTS', sub:`${oddities[i]} ${places[j]} is exactly where it was.`, weird:Math.min(.98,weird), weight:2.5, generated:true});
    n++;
  }
  return out;
})();
```
That's 150 + 150 = 300 generated encounters. Nice.

Then in main.js import ENCOUNTERS and use `const pool = EVENTS.concat(ENCOUNTERS).filter(...)`. Need to ensure triggerRandomEvent's switch default handles them (yes). But `state.stats.events` increments. Good.

However, many generated events with weird <= weird+.22 will flood at low weirdness (weird .1 → only weird<=.32, includes first ~40). That's fine, more variety.

Also, `ui.showEvent(ev.title, ev.sub)` displays. Good.

