content.text:
There's no explicit consent gate; the START button is disabled until boot completes but not gated by age confirmation. The summary said "18+ consent gate in menu" maybe intended. To meet the requirement robustly, add a consent step: when clicking START (new game), show a modal requiring "I AM 18 OR OLDER" / "EXIT". Only then start. But START currently directly startGame(false). We can implement a first-time gate stored in localStorage or session. Let's add:

- In bindEvents, btn-start click → if not acknowledged, show modal with actions "I AM 18 OR OLDER" (primary) and "LEAVE" (maybe title screen). On confirm, set consent flag and startGame(false).
- For CONTINUE, if save exists, allow without gate? Better require gate once per session. Use `let consentGiven = false;` and check.

But the modal is `ui.modal` and gameMode? At menu, gameMode is 'menu'; modal can show. onAction calls startGame(false).

Implement:
```
function requestConsent(then) {
  if (consentGiven) { then(); return; }
  gameMode = 'modal'; // but menu rendering pauses? loop menu path ignores gameMode. Modal overlay works.
  ui.modal({
    kicker:'MATURE CONTENT · 18+',
    title:'ARE YOU 18 OR OLDER?',
    body:'<p>...consensual, non-graphic...</p>',
    actions:[{label:'I AM 18 OR OLDER', id:'yes', primary:true},{label:'LEAVE', id:'no'}],
    onAction:(a)=>{ ui.closeModal(); if(a==='yes'){ consentGiven=true; then(); } else { gameMode='menu'; } }
  });
}
```
But `gameMode='modal'` while menu is showing: loop() has `if (gameMode === 'menu')` branch; if set to modal, it will go to paused branch and render world (fine) but menu remains visible behind modal. That's okay. However, `ui.modal` hides cinematic only. Menu stays. On close, set menu.

But if gameMode='modal', the menu branch is skipped, so world updates slowly; no issue.

Simpler: don't change gameMode; keep menu. Modal overlay sits above menu (z-index 65; menu z-index?). Menu likely z-index 50. Fine. Then on confirm, startGame sets play.

Let me add `let consentGiven = false;` near state vars, and gate both start and continue. Also persist consent in sessionStorage so reload doesn't re-prompt? Could use localStorage `bellingham_consent_v3` = '1'. But if user reloads, re-prompting is acceptable and safer. The requirement is a gate, not persistence. I'll use sessionStorage maybe. Simpler: module variable; each page load prompts once.

Need to make sure automated tests still work: our tests call `document.getElementById('btn-start').click()` which now opens a consent modal instead of starting. That would break all tests. We can expose a debug bypass or have the gate only show if `?nointro`? Better: expose `window.__BELLINGHAM` isn't available until boot; tests could click the consent button after. But all existing tests assume start immediately. We can update tests, but for final verification we'd need to adapt.

Alternative: gate via a checkbox in the menu that's already checked? That's not a real gate.

Given the user's requirement "18+ consent gate in menu", and the game is already clearly 18+, I think an explicit confirmation is worthwhile. I'll implement it and update the test helper to click the consent button if present. Since we've already verified systems, the final smoke test can handle it.

Implementation:
```
let consentGiven = false;
function requireConsent(then) {
  if (consentGiven) { then(); return; }
  ui.modal({
    kicker:'MATURE CONTENT · 18+',
    title:'BEFORE YOU CLOCK IN',
    body:`<p>...</p><p class="modal-quote">...</p>`,
    actions:[{label:'I AM 18 OR OLDER', id:'yes', primary:true},{label:'LEAVE', id:'no'}],
    onAction:(a)=>{ ui.closeModal(); if(a==='yes'){ consentGiven=true; then(); } }
  });
}
```
In bindEvents:
```
$('btn-start').addEventListener('click', () => { if (!$('btn-start').disabled) requireConsent(() => startGame(false)); });
$('btn-continue').addEventListener('click', () => requireConsent(() => startGame(true)));
```
But `ui.modal` may be hidden behind menu? z-index modal 65; menu z-index? Let me check `.screen` z-index. Search styles for #menu / .screen.

